{
  "_id": "phbrgrDreadAmbus",
  "name": "Dread Ambusher",
  "type": "feat",
  "folder": "de4kglc2V33iB0yi",
  "img": "icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-eyes-pink.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You have mastered the art of creating fearsome ambushes, granting you the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Ambusher’s Leap.</strong> At the start of your first turn of each combat, your Speed increases by 10 feet until the end of that turn.</p><p><strong>Dreadful Strike.</strong> When you attack a creature and hit it with a weapon, you can deal an extra 2d6 Psychic damage. You can use this benefit only once per turn, you can use it a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Initiative Bonus.</strong> When you roll Initiative, you can add your Wisdom modifier to the roll.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-QF11lzzOLRLzoSrk\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>This feature includes an Active Effect which automatically adds your Wisdom modifier to your Initiative roll.</p><p>The <strong>Dreadful Strike</strong> activity includes the additional damage and tracks your limited number of uses. It's damage will automatically increase when you gain the @UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.classes.Item.phbrgrStalkersFl]{Stalker's Flurry} feature.</p><p>The <strong>Ambusher's Leap</strong> activity includes an Active Effect that can be used to increase your Speed by 10 feet.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
